messages:
elaine: Hey all — found a parsing regression in the structured-output guide after #3421 merged. The function-calling example now produces an extra nested array for the tool output and the SDK parser bails.
omar: Ah. Which example file?
elaine: content/examples/function_calling/response-shapes.md ... line with the schema for `tool_result` — it uses `type: ["object", "array"]` and the client expects object only.
sam: Can we just normalize to always return an object with `items` when plural? E.g.
```
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "items": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
  },
  "required": ["items"]
}
```
omar: That'd be backward-incompatible for a few folks.
kevin: Proposal: docs should show both shapes and add a tiny migration snippet for the SDK to handle both. Keep canonical recommended schema = object-with-items and mark the array-only shape as legacy.
maggie: I can add an "Handling legacy array outputs" subsection and a TS snippet.
elaine: Great — also add a guardrail example using `oneOf` with explicit discriminator so LLM outputs prefer the object form. Tiny snippet:
```
"oneOf": [
  { "type": "object", "properties": {"items": {"type":"array"}}, "required":["items"]},
  {"type":"array", "items": {"type":"string"}}
]
```
sam: Nice. Also need to update SDK snippets: parsing helper in TS and Python. TS:
```ts
// normalizeToolResult.ts
export function normalizeToolResult(r: unknown): string[] {
  if (Array.isArray(r)) return r;
  if (r && typeof r === 'object' && 'items' in r) return (r as any).items;
  return [];
}
```
kevin: Can we add a tiny unit test in `docs-tests/schema-examples.test.ts`? Helps CI catch regressions.
docs-bot: Preview for PR #3427 ready: https://deploy-preview-3427--docs.redwood.ai
elaine: thanks — PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3427
omar: I'll take the docs review, want to make sure we add the link to the migration guide and update the TOC anchor.
maggie: Added both, plus a short note about prompt guardrails to prefer object outputs. Pushed commit.
kevin: left comments on the TS snippet — small typings cleanup, lgtm after that.
sam: once CI is green, can someone do a quick smoke on the SDK examples? I can run the TS helper locally.
elaine: tagging @omar for final sign-off :eyes:
omar: going to merge after tests — will squash-merge and add changelog entry.
elaine: thanks team :shipit:
